  Rodrigo Zepeda-Tello.

What is original here (not in bw)
  - The inversion (fit_pal): golden-section search over PAL against observed weights.
  - Bound-hit flags, input validation, the all-missing-weights guard.
  - The guard that drops the carbohydrate/sodium term of the ECF equation when the
    baseline-day carbohydrate intake is zero (upstream returns NaN there).
  - Tests, including parity tests against the `hallmodel` package (dev-only).

What is not ported
  - The child model, sodium-driven ECF changes (the sodium input is fixed at zero
    change), multi-individual matrices, intake interpolation (energy_build), and
    non-daily time steps.

